1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,430
Namaste. This is Liam, in for Bear. A long-running agent will tell you it's done.

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:07,397
The real question is how you make it prove it.

3
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:11,959
Three terms. The builder: the agent session that writes the feature. The evaluator:

4
00:00:11,979 --> 00:00:16,471
a separate agent that checks the work. And default-FAIL: every check starts as

5
00:00:16,491 --> 00:00:18,554
failing, until evidence proves it passes.

6
00:00:18,624 --> 00:00:23,294
Here's a long-running agent as a workshop. At the bench, a builder makes one feature

7
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:28,297
at a time. Left alone, it grades itself: after one unit test, it marks the part

8
00:00:28,317 --> 00:00:30,799
passing, even when the screen is visibly broken.

9
00:00:30,869 --> 00:00:35,688
Asking nicely doesn't reliably stop that. So the harness flips the default. Every

10
00:00:35,708 --> 00:00:40,527
feature is a row in test-results dot json, and every row starts false.

11
00:00:40,597 --> 00:00:45,534
A hook guards that file. The builder can't write to it until it has opened evidence:

12
00:00:45,554 --> 00:00:49,870
a screenshot, a console log. Each read unlocks one write. The next change needs

13
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:50,490
fresh proof.

14
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:54,937
Then a second agent inspects the work, from its own booth, with a fresh context. It

15
00:00:54,957 --> 00:00:59,610
never saw the build. It gets the spec, the diff and the screenshots, and it has no

16
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:00,709
Write or Edit tools.

17
00:01:00,779 --> 00:01:04,644
Its instructions say plausibility is not correctness, and missing evidence means

18
00:01:04,664 --> 00:01:10,294
needs work. So it answers PASS or needs work, and its findings become the next build

19
00:01:10,314 --> 00:01:11,354
session's first prompt.

20
00:01:11,424 --> 00:01:15,744
Each session starts cold. So the builder keeps its own handoff note, PROGRESS dot

21
00:01:15,764 --> 00:01:21,014
md, and reads it first on every restart. It commits as it goes, and a hook commits

22
00:01:21,034 --> 00:01:22,874
what's left when the session stops.

23
00:01:22,944 --> 00:01:27,745
Put it together and it's a loop: build, inspect, rebuild, until no row says false, a

24
00:01:27,765 --> 00:01:31,963
cycle changes nothing, or the budget runs out. Want true to mean the inspector

25
00:01:31,983 --> 00:01:34,373
agreed? Let only its PASS write the row.

26
00:01:34,443 --> 00:01:39,395
And you stay in charge. Create a file called agent stop, and every tool call halts.

27
00:01:39,415 --> 00:01:44,677
Write a note in STEER dot md, and the agent sees it once, mid-run, with no restart.

28
00:01:44,747 --> 00:01:49,146
Claude Code also has a built-in checker. Slash goal takes a condition, and after

29
00:01:49,166 --> 00:01:53,881
every turn a separate fast model checks it until it's met. Write your own evaluator

30
00:01:53,901 --> 00:01:57,669
dot md when you want your own inspector and the evidence gate.

31
00:01:57,739 --> 00:02:01,714
Your turn. Paste this into Claude Code: Help me write a default-FAIL evaluator for

32
00:02:01,734 --> 00:02:05,995
one long task: name your task. Save it as dot claude, slash agents, slash evaluator

33
00:02:06,015 --> 00:02:10,846
dot md, with no Write or Edit tools. List the exact conditions it must see to pass,

34
00:02:10,866 --> 00:02:15,126
and the evidence that proves each one: a screenshot, a console log, or a test

35
00:02:15,146 --> 00:02:19,121
result. It reviews only the spec, the diff and that evidence, never the builder's

36
00:02:19,141 --> 00:02:23,116
reasoning. Its first line is PASS or needs work; missing evidence is needs work.

37
00:02:23,136 --> 00:02:27,397
Don't build the task. Then check two things yourself. Hand it a commit with no

38
00:02:27,417 --> 00:02:31,677
screenshot. Does it say needs work? And open evaluator dot md. Does its tools line

39
00:02:31,697 --> 00:02:33,104
leave out Write and Edit?

40
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:37,645
The Inspector Says No First. At Nik Bear Brown.
